## Phase 2: LangGraph Orchestration (Completed)
We have successfully implemented the core multi-agent reasoning logic to convert prose text into an audio drama script!

- **Schemas & State:** Implemented the `Script` and `ScriptLine` schemas using Pydantic in [app/schemas/script.py](file:///c:/Users/Umesh%20Chandra/Desktop/Pocket_Forge/app/schemas/script.py), and defined our workflow graph state in [app/agents/state.py](file:///c:/Users/Umesh%20Chandra/Desktop/Pocket_Forge/app/agents/state.py).
- **Qdrant RAG Tool:** Created the `lore_rag_tool` inside [app/agents/tools.py](file:///c:/Users/Umesh%20Chandra/Desktop/Pocket_Forge/app/agents/tools.py) which embeds the character name and fetches their persona profile directly from the vector database.
- **LLM Configuration:** Configured Groq in [app/agents/llm.py](file:///c:/Users/Umesh%20Chandra/Desktop/Pocket_Forge/app/agents/llm.py) to point to the available `gpt-oss-20b` (for standard logic) and `gpt-oss-120b` (for complex, structured extraction).
- **Graph Nodes:** Implemented three agents inside [app/agents/nodes.py](file:///c:/Users/Umesh%20Chandra/Desktop/Pocket_Forge/app/agents/nodes.py):
  1. `Director Agent`: Breaks down a chapter to extract all speakers and a summary.
  2. `ScriptWriter Agent`: Looks up each speaker in the vector store and extracts a JSON-formatted script matching our Pydantic schema using `with_structured_output`.
  3. `Reviewer Agent`: Checks formatting and passes the script (or routes it back to the ScriptWriter for revisions).
- **StateGraph:** Wired the nodes together into a cyclical, conditional graph in [app/agents/graph.py](file:///c:/Users/Umesh%20Chandra/Desktop/Pocket_Forge/app/agents/graph.py).

> [!TIP]
> The LangGraph pipeline passed its automated verification. The agent successfully read the "Dr. Aris and Captain Vance" scene, generated an accurate breakdown, retrieved their personas, and generated the final `JSON` script with appropriate `emotion` tags!

## Phase 3: Celery Integration (Completed)
We have hooked up our FastAPI app to a background Celery worker to ensure our lengthy LLM audio generation doesn't block incoming web requests!

- **Worker Configuration**: The worker runs using the Redis broker we deployed via Docker.
- **Task Definition**: Refactored `app/worker/tasks.py` so that the `process_chapter_task` fetches the pending Postgres job asynchronously using `asyncio.run()`, runs the LangGraph pipeline, and writes the `script_json` back to the database.
- **API Endpoints**: 
    - `POST /upload-chapter`: Saves a job to Postgres as `Pending` and pushes it to Celery.
    - `GET /status/{job_id}`: Allows clients to poll for real-time status updates on their job.

> [!NOTE]
> I ran an end-to-end curl test on `/upload-chapter`. The Celery worker successfully picked it up, ran the LangGraph agent, and updated the Postgres job status to `processing_audio`!

## Phase 4: Audio Generation (Completed)
We implemented the final layer of our audio synthesis pipeline completely free of charge, avoiding any third party paid services like ElevenLabs.

- **Audio Service**: Created `app/services/audio.py` that utilizes Microsoft's `edge-tts` to map character personas to distinct, natural-sounding AI voices.
- **Idempotency & Concurrency**: Synthesizes each line concurrently using `asyncio.gather` for significantly faster generation while leveraging local caching (`chunk_{job_id}_{index}.mp3`) to prevent re-downloading existing audio.
- **Audio Merging**: Implemented a byte-level `.mp3` merging algorithm that concatenates all frames sequentially without relying on heavy external dependencies like `FFmpeg` or `pydub`. 
- **Static Delivery**: Merges the final output into `final_{job_id}.mp3` and serves it directly via FastAPI's `StaticFiles` mount at `/static/audio`.

> [!NOTE]
> I ran a final test, and the pipeline successfully processed the text, generated the chunks, merged them into a cohesive audio drama file, updated the PostgreSQL job status to `Completed`, and output a valid `result_audio_url`!

### 🎉 PocketForge is Complete!
PocketForge is now a fully functional, highly asynchronous, and free multi-agent AI pipeline for converting your web-novels into multi-voice audio dramas. The architecture robustly handles everything from queueing and graph orchestration to voice synthesis!
